## GitHub Flow

1. GitHub App receives webhook → git-bot validates HMAC.
2. git-bot fetches pipeline/triggers, creates/updates check run, posts run request to Nopsai.
3. Nopsai records run, checks AAA, resolves includes/variables/secrets, submits job to Dispatcher.
4. Dispatcher picks a runner (scope + least-active + routing).
5. Runner launches Agent, streams logs back, reports job status to Dispatcher, Agent reports task status to Nopsai/GitHub.
6. git-bot updates check runs with step/task progress, failures, and rerun/cancel actions; stale checks are cancelled.

