## Operations Tips

- Watch runner heartbeats in dispatcher logs; if missing >30s, dispatcher marks runner stale and requeues jobs.
- Ensure each runner has correct `RUNNER_SCOPES`; jobs without a matching runner will queue until a compatible runner connects.
- To add capacity, start additional runner containers pointing at the same dispatcher.
- If the core API restarts, running agents continue and will still post logs/status through the runner/dispatcher path.

---

## Security Notes

- Secrets stay encrypted at rest; logs are masked before leaving the agent.
- AAA denies before allows, logs denied decisions and sensitive allowed decisions, and is reachable only through the internal token-protected service interface.
- Use TLS/mTLS on gRPC endpoints in production (current defaults use insecure creds for local/dev).
- Protect the API/git-bot ingress with auth if exposed beyond trusted networks.

---

## Quick Commands

- Compose up: `docker-compose up --build -d`
- Tail dispatcher: `docker logs -f nopsai-dispatcher`
- Tail runner: `docker logs -f nopsai-runner`
- Trigger config sync: `curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/v1/internal/config/sync`

With these pieces, Nopsai now follows a standard CI/CD control-plane/data-plane pattern similar to GitHub Actions or GitLab Runners, making it easier to scale and to place runners near your workloads.
